Z||000000||FiXXXerX||12-22-2001||11:44 AM||||I got a 1986 Fiero 2M4 for $200 from a guy who didn't know better, the car itself did not run, but he said it was a fuel problem, so, naturally, I bought the car, brought it home and started working on it, first tearing out everything that was on the interior, and cleaning it out. Second, I dropped the tank to remove the sender unit and install a new fuel pump (The guy had installed the fuel pump end-line near the carb, and had rigged this up himself.... needless to say this DID NOT WORK) so, I went and took the sender unit out, but when I did, to my horror, the whole unit was rusted, and.... well.... ummm.... "Intrestingly Engineered", but I dunno what I exepected from a guy who was holding the gas tank in with kitchen ties, so, I located a new sender unit from the Junkyard, installed it, made sure it pumped gas, and then proceeded to repair the fuel line. Now, I've done all of this, and its getting extreme backpressure, and causes leaks in the line, so, I traced it back to the Carb unit and found that it gets into it, just not out of it, I think it might be a TBI Unit, anyone else have any Ideas? I'm pretty sure it is, but, I've never worked with a fiero before, or a TBI/TPI or Fuel Injected car before.<P>Adam||||reg||3
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||12-22-2001||11:57 AM||||Sorry, I cant help much. I just found it funny how simmilar my fieros fuel system seems to be to yours   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>If your not geting any fuel at all try hot wiring a 12V ground to the injector (make sure you do it right as to not short anything out, I beleave 12V pos is allways ran to the injector). My fiero *sometimes* wont fire the injector unless I prime the engine first and start it. I've looked around this fiero forum and found this might be a common problum maybe with the ECM. So I have a button wired that jumps ground to it when needed. Good luck, hope this maybe somewhat helps.<P>EDIT- Coffee not stong enough  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 12-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-22-2001||11:58 AM||||Adam,<P>This car should only run max of 12psi fuel pressure.  If the line is leaking it should not be from anything but ......well a leaking line.  See if fuel sprays when you turn the engine over...from the injector.  If it does then that is first problem solved.  But, make sure you don't have any leaks in the lines.  Glad to help....just let me know...got 25 years experience.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||4
Z||000003||theogre||12-22-2001||12:05 PM||||Are you sure the lines aren't crossed? The fuel pressure regulator is a one way device.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||ITB 2M4||12-22-2001||12:14 PM||||Hey FiXXXerX, good to see somebody from Ft. Misery on the board!  I'm not REAL familiar with TBI, but I've been around it enough to figure out what needs to be replaced.  Either reply here, e-mail me, or send a PM, and I'll get back to you.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||10
Z||000005||FiXXXerX||12-22-2001||12:23 PM||||Ok, sorry to confuse, probobly should add this part, yes, there was a leak in the return fuel line, I've pretty much fixed it. When I turn the engine over, or try to, fuel does pump out and quite well I might add  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>So, basicly whats happening is nothing is coming out of the TBI unit.... it does go into the carb though, and over that bridge to the TBI unit, I've take the carb apart to see this. it just doesn't get any farther.<P>Adam<P>------------------<BR>-= If the Front wheels don't leave the ground, its still broken =-||||reg||3
